<title>SOUTH KOREA: KOREA GREEN CROSS INTERIM NET JUMPS.</title>
<headline>KOREA GREEN CROSS INTERIM NET JUMPS.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>	 (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				 1,265    vs   649</p>
<p>    Net					     3.17 vs     1.51</p>
<p>    Turnover				    100.89 vs    96.61</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			   4.93 vs     2.71</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (both loss)	     3.30 vs     0.40</p>
<p>Note - Korea Green Cross Corp is a South Korean pharmaceutical firm. Its net profit surged on a drop in production and sales costs and general administration expenses, a company official said. Its share capital increased to 2.65 million at the end of June from 2.49 million a year ago due to dividend payments and bond conversions.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
